# Exported so //glean/glass/test/regression:glass-regression-cpp (a
# different buck2 package) can embed the same two files, matching Cabal's
# own model exactly: glass-regression-cpp's own stanza (glean.cabal.in)
# lists `Glean.Clang.Test`/`Glean.Clang.Test.DerivePass` as `other-modules`
# too, recompiled fresh there rather than shared via a library, the same
# duplication already used across all 6 `clang-test-*` targets above.
# buck2 (unlike Cabal) requires a file to belong to exactly one package,
# so it can't just be listed as a raw `srcs` path from the other package -
# `export_file()` re-exposes it as a target these two consumers can
# reference directly (`_resolve_src` in buck2/haskell.bzl already treats
# a dict `srcs` value that isn't a local path as something to relocate via
# `export_file()`, and `export_file()`'s own `src` attr accepts a
# cross-package dependency just as well as a local file).
native.export_file(
    name = "test-hs",
    src = "Glean/Clang/Test.hs",
    visibility = ["PUBLIC"],
)

native.export_file(
    name = "test-derivepass-hs",
    src = "Glean/Clang/Test/DerivePass.hs",
    visibility = ["PUBLIC"],
)
